---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import '../styles/global.css';
---

<Layout title="Protect PLG — Prospect Lefferts Gardens">

<!-- ─── HERO ─── -->
<section class="hero">
  <Nav activePage="home" />

  <div class="hero-body">
    <p class="eyebrow"><span>Prospect Lefferts Gardens, Brooklyn</span></p>
    <h1 class="hero-headline">
      Protect <em>PLG.</em>
    </h1>
    <p class="hero-sub">
      Development accountability, affordable housing, and community participation.
    </p>
    <div class="hero-ctas">
      <a href="#join" class="btn-primary">Join the Effort</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ─── OUR ASKS ─── -->
<section class="about" id="asks">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="about-body reveal" style="max-width:760px;">
      <p class="section-label">What We're Asking For</p>
      <h2 class="section-title">The same deal, <em>every time.</em></h2>
      <p>Prospect Lefferts Gardens keeps absorbing large new buildings that are decided with little public notice and no enforceable affordability. Whatever gets built, and wherever, we are asking for the same things:</p>
    </div>

    <ul class="facts-list reveal" style="margin-top:2.5rem;">
      <li><span class="fact-icon">⬤</span><div><span class="fact-strong">Accurate, current information</span> about approved development plans, made available to the public.</div></li>
      <li><span class="fact-icon">⬤</span><div><span class="fact-strong">A full review of zoning and permitting</span> &mdash; FAR calculations, open-space ratios, and any air-rights transfers &mdash; confirmed by DOB and DCP.</div></li>
      <li><span class="fact-icon">⬤</span><div><span class="fact-strong">Meaningful, enforceable affordable housing</span>, with terms in writing, rather than vague commitments.</div></li>
      <li><span class="fact-icon">⬤</span><div><span class="fact-strong">Direct dialogue</span> among landowners, developers, elected officials, and the community.</div></li>
      <li><span class="fact-icon">⬤</span><div><span class="fact-strong">A tangible community benefit</span> from each development for the block and the neighborhood.</div></li>
      <li><span class="fact-icon">⬤</span><div><span class="fact-strong">Contextual zoning for PLG</span>, so future development is built to a predictable scale.</div></li>
      <li><span class="fact-icon">⬤</span><div><span class="fact-strong">A clear public record</span> of how each project was reviewed and approved.</div></li>
    </ul>

    <div class="housing-position reveal">
      <p class="section-label" style="margin-bottom:0.8rem;">Where We Stand on Housing</p>
      <p>We support the creation of new housing, including greater density where appropriate. We are asking that development comply fully with applicable requirements, include meaningful affordable housing, and provide a clear public benefit to the community affected by it.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ─── WHY DOES THIS KEEP HAPPENING ─── -->
<section class="about" id="why" style="background:var(--black); border-top:1px solid rgba(200,40,26,0.2); border-bottom:1px solid rgba(200,40,26,0.2);">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="about-body reveal" style="max-width:800px;">
      <p class="section-label">The Bigger Picture</p>
      <h2 class="section-title">Why does this <em>keep happening?</em></h2>
      <p>Prospect Lefferts Gardens' zoning was last comprehensively updated in <strong>1961</strong>. Most of the neighborhood is zoned R6 &mdash; a 1960s "Tower in the Park" framework with a floor-area ratio of 2.43 and <strong>no height limit</strong>. On PLG's large lots, that math rewards demolishing smaller buildings and replacing them with much bigger ones.</p>
      <p>The neighborhood has been formally asking the Department of City Planning for a <strong>contextual rezoning study since 2008</strong>. Park Slope, Windsor Terrace, and Kensington all received contextual zoning with height limits years ago. PLG did not.</p>
      <p>PLG has added thousands of units over the past decade, much of it market-rate, with one-bedrooms renting for $3,000&ndash;$4,000 a month. The gap here is affordability and predictability &mdash; not raw supply.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="about-body reveal" style="max-width:800px; margin-top:2.5rem;">
      <p class="section-label" style="margin-bottom:0.8rem;">How the Process Works</p>
    </div>
    <ul class="facts-list reveal">
      <li><span class="fact-icon">⬤</span><div><span class="fact-strong">As-of-right building.</span> If a project fits the existing zoning, the developer can build it with DOB permits alone &mdash; no public hearing, no City Council vote.</div></li>
      <li><span class="fact-icon">⬤</span><div><span class="fact-strong">DOB review.</span> The Department of Buildings checks plans against the zoning and building code, including FAR, open space, and any air-rights transfers. Its records are public, but not always easy to read.</div></li>
      <li><span class="fact-icon">⬤</span><div><span class="fact-strong">ULURP.</span> The Uniform Land Use Review Procedure is the public process &mdash; community board, borough president, City Planning Commission, City Council. It is only triggered when a project needs a zoning change, variance, or special permit. An as-of-right building skips it entirely.</div></li>
      <li><span class="fact-icon">⬤</span><div><span class="fact-strong">Contextual rezoning.</span> A neighborhood-wide zoning change, run through ULURP, is the tool that would set predictable height and setback rules for future projects across PLG.</div></li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ─── THE 331 MAPLE STREET CASE ─── -->
<section class="about" id="case">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="before-after reveal">
      <div class="ba-card">
        <div class="ba-label ba-label-before">Demolished, 2026</div>
        <img src="/331mapleparish.png" alt="The former parish school at 335 Maple St, built 1909" />
        <p class="ba-caption">The 335 Maple St parish school, built 1909. Demolished in 2026.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="ba-arrow">→</div>
      <div class="ba-card">
        <div class="ba-label ba-label-after">Under construction</div>
        <img src="/331maplemockup.png" alt="Developer rendering of the building at 331 Maple St" />
        <p class="ba-caption">Developer rendering of the 12-story, 118-foot, 99-unit building now under construction. Affordability terms have not been made public.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="about-body reveal" style="max-width:800px; margin-top:4rem;">
      <p class="section-label">The 331 Maple Street Case</p>
      <h2 class="section-title">How one project <em>unfolded.</em></h2>
      <p>The clearest recent example is 331&ndash;335 Maple Street. The land is owned by the Roman Catholic parish of St. Francis of Assisi and St. Blaise, which signed a long-term ground lease with developer <strong>Candor Capital</strong>. In August 2025, plans were filed with the Department of Buildings for a 12-story, 118-foot building with 99 apartments and about 24,000 square feet of community-facility space, on an R6 lot <span class="cite">(<a href="https://commercialobserver.com/2025/08/candor-capital-housing-331-maple-street-brooklyn/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Commercial Observer</a>, <a href="https://brooklyneagle.com/articles/2025/08/22/brooklyn-developer-files-plans-for-99-apartments-on-church-owned-lot" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Brooklyn Eagle</a>, <a href="https://newyorkyimby.com/2025/09/permits-filed-for-331-maple-street-in-prospect-lefferts-gardens-brooklyn.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">NY YIMBY</a>)</span>.</p>
      <p>According to Father Thomas Vassalotti, church leadership was shown a six-story concept before the lease was signed; the plans filed with DOB were for twelve stories. Because the project is largely as-of-right, there was no public hearing.</p>
      <p>In January 2026, demolition activity began at 335 Maple Street before the required permits were issued. DOB issued a <strong>Stop Work Order</strong>, and the developer went on to receive violations and fines totaling roughly <strong>$30,000</strong>. The 1909 parish school was demolished later that year, and construction is now underway.</p>
      <p>Questions about the project's zoning basis remain open. Community members who have reviewed ACRIS records have not identified a recorded air-rights transfer between the development lot and the larger church lot that would support the building's floor area. Residents have asked DOB and City Planning to confirm the FAR calculation and publish the review. Affordability terms for the building have not been made public.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ─── NEIGHBOR QUOTES ─── -->
<section class="quotes-strip">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="quotes-header reveal">
      <p class="section-label" style="color:rgba(245,239,224,0.4);">In Their Own Words</p>
      <h2 class="section-title">Real neighbors. <em>Real stakes.</em></h2>
    </div>
    <div class="quotes-grid">
      <blockquote class="pull-quote reveal">
        <p>"The amount of development I've seen without consulting the local community has only resulted in 'affordable' apartments that locals can't afford, resulting in a money grab by developers while destroying the local neighborhood. We need to have a discussion about what our future can look like."</p>
        <footer><strong>Diana</strong><span>Midwood Street</span></footer>
      </blockquote>
      <blockquote class="pull-quote reveal">
        <p>"We need all new housing built with contextual height restrictions to respect and preserve the existing neighborhoods. This proposed building violates the neighborhood context and would significantly change the nature of this neighborhood detrimentally."</p>
        <footer><strong>Margaret</strong><span>Midwood Street</span></footer>
      </blockquote>
      <blockquote class="pull-quote reveal">
        <p>"We need affordable housing, not high-rises. Don't destroy the neighborhood."</p>
        <footer><strong>Benjamin</strong><span>Snyder Avenue</span></footer>
      </blockquote>
    </div>
    <div class="quotes-cta reveal">
      <a href="/voices" class="btn-outline">Read All Neighbor Voices →</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ─── CENTRAL MESSAGE ─── -->
<section class="creed-section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="creed reveal">
      <p>Prospect Lefferts Gardens keeps getting the same deal: big buildings, short notice, no enforceable affordability. <em>Protect PLG</em> works to change how those decisions get made &mdash; one project at a time, and neighborhood-wide.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ─── JOIN THE EFFORT ─── -->
<section class="join-section" id="join">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="reveal">
      <p class="section-label">Join the Effort</p>
      <h2 class="section-title">Add your name. <em>Lend a hand.</em></h2>
      <p class="join-intro">Protect PLG runs on neighbors showing up for each other &mdash; canvassing, showing up to meetings, digging through records, and spreading the word. Tell us how you can help and we'll be in touch.</p>
    </div>

    <form id="join-form" class="join-form reveal" action="https://api.web3forms.com/submit" method="POST">
      <input type="hidden" name="access_key" value="207bb50e-9621-42c1-bafe-c8887e520c31" />
      <input type="hidden" name="subject" value="New Protect PLG signup" />
      <input type="hidden" name="from_name" value="Protect PLG website" />
      <input type="checkbox" name="botcheck" class="join-hp" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off" aria-hidden="true" />

      <div class="join-field">
        <label for="join-name">Name</label>
        <input type="text" id="join-name" name="name" required autocomplete="name" />
      </div>

      <div class="join-field">
        <label for="join-email">Email</label>
        <input type="email" id="join-email" name="email" required autocomplete="email" />
      </div>

      <fieldset class="join-field join-check-group">
        <legend class="join-legend">How I can help</legend>
        <label class="join-check"><input type="checkbox" name="help" value="Canvassing" /> Canvassing</label>
        <label class="join-check"><input type="checkbox" name="help" value="Attending meetings" /> Attending meetings</label>
        <label class="join-check"><input type="checkbox" name="help" value="Research" /> Research</label>
        <label class="join-check"><input type="checkbox" name="help" value="Outreach" /> Outreach</label>
      </fieldset>

      <div class="join-field">
        <label for="join-message">Message <span style="text-transform:none; letter-spacing:0;">(optional)</span></label>
        <textarea id="join-message" name="message"></textarea>
      </div>

      <button type="submit" class="btn-primary join-submit">Join the Effort</button>
      <p class="join-error" id="join-error" hidden>Something went wrong sending that. Please try again in a moment.</p>
    </form>

    <div class="join-success" id="join-success" hidden>
      <p><strong>Thanks &mdash; you're on the list.</strong> We'll reach out with next steps and meeting information.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<Footer />

<script>
  // Join form — submit to Web3Forms via fetch, show inline success state
  const form = document.getElementById('join-form') as HTMLFormElement | null;
  if (form) {
    const errBox = document.getElementById('join-error');
    const successBox = document.getElementById('join-success');
    const submitBtn = form.querySelector('button[type="submit"]') as HTMLButtonElement | null;
    form.addEventListener('submit', async (e) => {
      e.preventDefault();
      if (errBox) errBox.hidden = true;
      if (submitBtn) { submitBtn.disabled = true; submitBtn.textContent = 'Sending…'; }
      try {
        const res = await fetch(form.action, {
          method: 'POST',
          body: new FormData(form),
          headers: { Accept: 'application/json' },
        });
        const data = await res.json();
        if (res.ok && data.success) {
          form.hidden = true;
          if (successBox) successBox.hidden = false;
          successBox?.scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth', block: 'center' });
        } else {
          throw new Error(data.message || 'Request failed');
        }
      } catch {
        if (submitBtn) { submitBtn.disabled = false; submitBtn.textContent = 'Join the Effort'; }
        if (errBox) errBox.hidden = false;
      }
    });
  }

  // Scroll reveal
  document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
    const els = document.querySelectorAll('.reveal');
    if (!('IntersectionObserver' in window)) { els.forEach(el => el.classList.add('visible')); return; }
    const obs = new IntersectionObserver((entries, o) => {
      entries.forEach(e => { if (e.isIntersecting) { e.target.classList.add('visible'); o.unobserve(e.target); } });
    }, { threshold: 0.08 });
    els.forEach(el => obs.observe(el));
  });
</script>

</Layout>

<style is:global>
  .hero {
    background: var(--black);
    position: relative;
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .hero::before { content: ''; position: absolute; inset: 0; background: radial-gradient(ellipse 80% 60% at 50% 120%, #C8281A22 0%, transparent 70%); pointer-events: none; }
  .hero::after { content: ''; position: absolute; inset: 0; background-image: url("data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg viewBox='0 0 256 256' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%3E%3Cfilter id='noise'%3E%3CfeTurbulence type='fractalNoise' baseFrequency='0.9' numOctaves='4' stitchTiles='stitch'/%3E%3C/filter%3E%3Crect width='100%25' height='100%25' filter='url(%23noise)' opacity='0.06'/%3E%3C/svg%3E"); pointer-events: none; opacity: 0.4; }
  .hero-body { display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; justify-content: center; text-align: center; padding: 5.5rem 2rem 5rem; position: relative; z-index: 5; }
  .eyebrow { font-size: 0.72rem; letter-spacing: 0.22em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--red); margin-bottom: 1.5rem; animation: fadeUp 0.8s ease both; }
  .eyebrow span { display: inline-block; background: rgba(200,40,26,0.15); border: 1px solid rgba(200,40,26,0.4); padding: 0.3rem 0.9rem; border-radius: 2px; }
  .hero-headline { font-family: 'Bebas Neue', sans-serif; font-size: clamp(3.5rem, 11vw, 9rem); line-height: 0.92; letter-spacing: 0.02em; animation: fadeUp 0.8s 0.15s ease both; }
  .hero-headline em { font-style: normal; color: var(--red); display: block; }
  .hero-sub { max-width: 640px; margin: 2rem auto 0; font-size: 1.15rem; line-height: 1.65; color: rgba(245,239,224,0.7); animation: fadeUp 0.8s 0.3s ease both; }
  .hero-sub strong { color: var(--cream); font-weight: 500; }
  .hero-ctas { display: flex; gap: 1rem; margin-top: 2.5rem; flex-wrap: wrap; justify-content: center; animation: fadeUp 0.8s 0.45s ease both; align-items: center; }

  /* ─── QUOTES STRIP ─── */
  .quotes-strip { background: rgba(245,239,224,0.03); border-top: 1px solid rgba(245,239,224,0.07); border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(245,239,224,0.07); padding: 5rem 2rem; }
  .quotes-header { text-align: center; margin-bottom: 3rem; }
  .quotes-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 2rem; }
  .pull-quote { margin: 0; padding: 2rem; background: rgba(245,239,224,0.04); border: 1px solid rgba(245,239,224,0.08); border-top: 3px solid var(--red); display: flex; flex-direction: column; justify-content: space-between; gap: 1.5rem; }
  .pull-quote p { font-family: 'DM Serif Display', serif; font-style: italic; font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.7; color: rgba(245,239,224,0.8); margin: 0; }
  .pull-quote footer { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.2rem; }
  .pull-quote footer strong { font-size: 0.88rem; font-weight: 500; color: var(--cream); font-style: normal; }
  .pull-quote footer span { font-size: 0.73rem; color: rgba(245,239,224,0.4); letter-spacing: 0.06em; }
  .quotes-cta { text-align: center; margin-top: 3rem; }
  @media (max-width: 900px) { .quotes-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; max-width: 560px; margin: 0 auto; } }

  .about { background: var(--warm-gray); padding-top: 4rem; padding-bottom: 4rem; }
  .about-body p { color: rgba(245,239,224,0.72); line-height: 1.75; margin-bottom: 1.2rem; font-size: 1.02rem; }
  .about-body strong { color: var(--cream); font-weight: 500; }
  .about-body a { color: rgba(200,40,26,0.95); text-decoration: none; }
  .about-body a:hover { color: var(--accent); }
  .cite { font-size: 0.9rem; color: rgba(245,239,224,0.5); }
  .facts-list { list-style: none; display: flex; flex-direction: column; }
  .facts-list li { padding: 1.1rem 0; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(245,239,224,0.1); display: flex; gap: 1rem; align-items: flex-start; font-size: 0.95rem; color: rgba(245,239,224,0.7); line-height: 1.55; }
  .facts-list li:first-child { border-top: 1px solid rgba(245,239,224,0.1); }
  .fact-icon { color: var(--red); font-size: 0.7rem; margin-top: 0.38rem; flex-shrink: 0; }
  .fact-strong { color: var(--cream); font-weight: 500; }

  .housing-position { background: rgba(245,239,224,0.04); border: 1px solid rgba(245,239,224,0.12); border-left: 4px solid var(--red); padding: 1.8rem 2rem; margin-top: 3rem; max-width: 760px; }
  .housing-position p:last-child { color: rgba(245,239,224,0.8); line-height: 1.75; font-size: 1.02rem; }

  .before-after { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr auto 1fr; gap: 1.5rem; align-items: center; }
  .ba-card { position: relative; overflow: hidden; }
  .ba-card img { width: 100%; height: 320px; object-fit: cover; display: block; filter: brightness(0.9); }
  .ba-label { position: absolute; top: 1rem; left: 1rem; font-size: 0.65rem; letter-spacing: 0.16em; text-transform: uppercase; padding: 0.3rem 0.8rem; z-index: 2; font-weight: 500; }
  .ba-label-before { background: rgba(14,14,14,0.85); color: var(--cream); border: 1px solid rgba(245,239,224,0.3); }
  .ba-label-after { background: rgba(200,40,26,0.9); color: #fff; }
  .ba-caption { font-size: 0.75rem; color: rgba(245,239,224,0.45); padding: 0.7rem 0 0; line-height: 1.4; font-style: italic; }
  .ba-arrow { font-size: 2.5rem; color: var(--red); opacity: 0.6; font-family: 'Bebas Neue', sans-serif; text-align: center; }

  .creed-section { background: var(--cream); color: var(--black); padding: 6rem 2rem; }
  .creed { max-width: 820px; margin: 0 auto; text-align: center; }
  .creed p { font-family: 'DM Serif Display', serif; font-size: clamp(1.4rem, 3vw, 2.1rem); line-height: 1.45; color: var(--black); }
  .creed em { font-style: italic; color: var(--dark-red); }

  /* ─── JOIN FORM ─── */
  .join-section { background: var(--black); border-top: 1px solid rgba(200,40,26,0.2); }
  .join-intro { color: rgba(245,239,224,0.55); max-width: 640px; line-height: 1.7; margin-top: 0.5rem; }
  .join-form { max-width: 620px; margin-top: 2.75rem; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1.4rem; }
  .join-field { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.45rem; border: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; }
  .join-field label, .join-legend { font-size: 0.72rem; letter-spacing: 0.14em; text-transform: uppercase; color: rgba(245,239,224,0.5); padding: 0; }
  .join-field input[type="text"], .join-field input[type="email"], .join-field textarea {
    background: rgba(245,239,224,0.04); border: 1px solid rgba(245,239,224,0.18); color: var(--cream);
    padding: 0.8rem 0.95rem; font-family: 'DM Sans', sans-serif; font-size: 0.98rem; border-radius: 2px; width: 100%;
  }
  .join-field input:focus, .join-field textarea:focus { outline: none; border-color: var(--red); background: rgba(245,239,224,0.06); }
  .join-field textarea { min-height: 110px; resize: vertical; }
  .join-check-group { gap: 0.75rem; margin-top: 0.3rem; }
  .join-check { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.65rem; font-size: 0.98rem; color: rgba(245,239,224,0.8); letter-spacing: 0; text-transform: none; cursor: pointer; }
  .join-check input { width: 1.05rem; height: 1.05rem; accent-color: var(--red); flex-shrink: 0; }
  .join-hp { position: absolute !important; left: -9999px !important; opacity: 0 !important; height: 0; width: 0; }
  .join-submit { align-self: flex-start; margin-top: 0.4rem; }
  .join-submit:disabled { opacity: 0.6; cursor: default; transform: none; }
  .join-error { background: rgba(200,40,26,0.12); border: 1px solid rgba(200,40,26,0.45); color: #f2c9c3; padding: 0.9rem 1.1rem; font-size: 0.9rem; border-radius: 2px; }
  .join-success { background: rgba(34,197,94,0.1); border: 1px solid rgba(34,197,94,0.4); border-left: 4px solid #22c55e; color: #d7f5e0; padding: 1.6rem 1.8rem; margin-top: 2.5rem; max-width: 620px; line-height: 1.6; }
  .join-success strong { color: #fff; }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .before-after { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .ba-arrow { transform: rotate(90deg); text-align: center; }
    .ba-card img { height: 240px; }
  }
  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .hero-body { padding: 3rem 1.2rem 2.5rem; }
    .hero-ctas { flex-direction: column; align-items: stretch; }
    .about { padding-top: 2.5rem; padding-bottom: 2.5rem; }
  }
  @media (max-width: 400px) {
    .hero-sub { font-size: 1rem; }
  }
</style>
